module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.estimated_footprint_or_kv_per_token_used_as_a_wall

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data estimated_footprint_or_kv_per_token_used_as_a_wall: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "estimated_footprint_or_kv_per_token_used_as_a_wall" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: an estimated model footprint or KV-per-token figure is consumed as a hard fit wall. HARM: a launch that would have fit (or would not) is refused or admitted against a number nobody measured, and gunbc.design_argument::epistemic_humility is violated: an inference is treated as a deduced fact. DISTINGUISHING FACT: vLLM 'Model loading took' is an allocation delta, not checkpoint tensor bytes; KV bytes per token are an observation of a launch, not a datasheet identity. SPECIMEN: 69 GiB estimated versus 80.1 GiB measured model-load allocation; 24.6 versus ~31 KB/token. RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable, caught in design review 2026-10-12. CEILING: mechanically preventable once P3 receipts carry measured allocation and measured KV capacity and P4 fit reads those, never the estimate, as the wall. NEXT TRIGGER: P4 feasibility consumes observed model-load GPU allocation per rank and measured KV capacity. CONSUMPTION: P4 home-serving feasibility.",
    "PXE 2c lane 2026-11-12 (wise-otter-90, 24 GiB cgroup; warm-raven-804 fix): the v1 typed-module cache's ENTRY CAP was the wall — cache_entries = host budget / TYPED_MODULE_BYTES_PER_ENTRY_ESTIMATE (a declared Scaffold `interim declared denominator until measured space lands`, 3 MiB) clamped to a constant ceiling. The estimate under-counted the true per-entry footprint ~6.7x (a module measured ~20 MiB), so the entry-count wall admitted ~6.7x the working set the envelope could hold and the run was refused ONLY as page-grain thrash (gunbc.host.memory_stall_refusal MemoryStallRefusedPageThrash, ~35k major faults/min at 3% CPU; the module states the count is blind to it: 'the thrash is at PAGE grain underneath the allocator, invisible to entry counts'). GUNBC_TYPED_MODULE_CACHE_MAX_ENTRIES=450 (an operator hand-picking a number at the measured link) completed cleanly — the tell that the wall's authority sat in the wrong place. Repair (warm-raven-804): the entry count is demoted to a non-authoritative backstop (the 3 MiB estimate is left untouched so NO new footprint estimate is adopted) and the OBSERVED budget the cap was already denominated in becomes a live resident-set bound — when THIS process's own resident footprint reaches 8750 bp of the observed budget the cache YIELDS entries until resident recedes to 8000 bp (gunbc.typed_module_cache_capacity resident_exceeds_cache_pressure_line / resident_recedes_below_cache_pressure_line), authority = the host/slot memory envelope (gunbc.host.memory_envelope / gunbc.runner.runner_slot_desired), only ever lowering. A naive drain-to-the-floor on crossing 8750 bp was itself a defect (review 94312): glibc keeps freed arenas resident so VmRSS does not fall when entries drop, the gated signal sticks high, and the cache pins at the floor becoming a churn machine. The two things that make the yield real: malloc_trim after each yield batch (measured: drop without trim leaves VmRSS unchanged, with trim it collapses) and a release line BELOW the trigger (a hysteresis band) so a yield that lands in the band disarms instead of re-triggering every insert. General form shared with the vllm-002 specimen: a resource cap whose per-unit size is an estimate, consumed as the wall, refused only when the workload outgrew it.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
